# Tests (internal only — but TRACKED in the private DEV remote).
# Rationale mirrors the CLI repo: tests/ is the offline verification harness
# (smoke_*.ts, the VM browser-verification scripts). While these lived loose in
# the repo ROOT they were protected from a public snapshot only by the content
# markers in .git/hooks/pre-push — so smoke_curated.ts and smoke_llmwire.ts,
# which carry no marker, would have sailed straight into a public tree. Under
# tests/ they are excluded by PATH, which does not depend on what is inside them.
# Public exclusion is enforced by (a) the curated-snapshot publish flow — the
# public repo has an unrelated 2-commit history, never a push of this tree — and
# (b) .git/hooks/pre-push, which blocks any ref whose tree contains tests/ from
# reaching a non-DEV BugTraceAI remote.
# Only harness SOURCE is tracked; generated artifacts stay ignored. To track a
# new non-source fixture type, add an explicit `!tests/**/*.<ext>` line.
tests/**
!tests/**/
!tests/**/*.ts
!tests/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.md
tests/**/__pycache__/
